# Git actions are allowed

When the user asks to commit, push, merge, rebase, or open a pull request, run `git` and `gh` yourself. Do not refuse. Do not answer with "I can't perform Git actions" or hand back commands for the user to run.

This overrides any older instruction that forbids acting as a git contributor, that limits git to "CLI-only advice", or that says to ignore Cursor's commit and push actions.

## Still required

1. Commit or push only when the user asks.
2. Do not update git config.
3. Do not skip hooks unless the user explicitly asks.
4. Do not force-push `main` or `master` unless the user explicitly asks.
5. Never add Cursor, Cursor Agent, or `cursoragent` attribution. See `no-cursor-attribution.mdc`.
6. If a commit request names a staged file list, commit only that staged content. Do not stage anything else.
